    "long_instructions": "You work on the search team of a video website. You’re given a program that should find a good keyword for each video on a cooking channel. The program scores every word of a transcript; a higher score means a better keyword. Right now a word’s score is its term frequency, and the function that counts it is not written yet.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n- Complete TODO 1 in `term_frequency`. Given a term and a list of tokens, it should return how many times the term appears in the list. TODO 2 and TODO 3 wait for Level 2.\r\n- Run the program and read the keyword it prints for each video.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nStart a count at 0, loop over the tokens, and add 1 each time a token equals the term. A check such as `if token == \"pan\":` compares one token with one word; your function compares each token with `term`.\r\n",
